      "content": "From a rigorous ethical standpoint, I would argue that in cases where a government is poised to commit atrocities, it may be morally justifiable to take preemptive action to prevent harm. This approach prioritizes the prevention of harm to civilians above state sovereignty and territorial integrity, aligning with a consequentialist view that would evaluate the prevent-then-regret calculus as morally superior to the past-then-regret calculus often underlying traditional just war doctrine.",
